            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical approach in vulvar cancer surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vulva cancer is rare. It is mainly treated through surgery. Recurrent scarring complications can prolong the period of hospitalisation. To reduce scar dihiscence, the nursing team of the Oscar Lambret Centre in Lille treats scars by negative pressure as a preventative measure. It also integrates into its clinical approach the prevention of pain and malnutrition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
